title: Git.pm still documents the ssh:// timeout gap that the 1.9.3 floor closed
updated: 2026-08-18T04:38:56Z
---

Follow-up to #174, which closed the ssh:// hang by pinning Alien::Libgit2
0.002 (pkg-config floor libgit2 1.9.3, the release carrying PR #7165). The
dependency now guarantees a libgit2 whose ssh transport honours
GIT_OPT_SET_SERVER_TIMEOUT, but four places in lib/App/karr/Git.pm still tell
the reader the opposite:

  * POD ~L60-66: "libgit2 applies it to its own socket transports (git://,
    http://, https://), not to ssh://, whose reads go through libssh2" --
    no longer true from 1.9.3 up.
  * Comment ~L289-292: "an ssh:// remote still hangs the native path [...]
    only bounded route for ssh".
  * Comment ~L1409-1415 (remote_has_board): "cannot be bounded for ssh:// --
    libssh2 retries past libgit2s socket timeout [...] (#174, measured)".
  * POD ~L1472-1474: for ssh:// the CLI is described as the only route.

The POD text is the smaller half. The real question is remote_has_board: it
deliberately skips the native transport altogether, and the reason given is
exactly the gap that is now closed. With the floor in place that argument no
longer holds, so either the native path becomes admissible there again -- it
runs unasked in front of every read command (#173), so the cost is a fork per
call -- or the CLI-only choice needs a reason that survives 1.9.3.

Deliberately left alone while closing #174: that ticket was decided as "no
transport policy change, no version switch in App::karr::Git", and reopening
remote_has_board is a policy change. It wants its own decision.

Also worth having: t/170-native-transport-timeout.t states in its header that
it uses git:// rather than ssh:// "because the ssh case does not come back".
With the floor it does come back, so the ssh case can finally be a regression
test -- guarded by a skip on Git::Libgit2::version() < 1.9.3 for anyone
running against an older system lib on purpose.
Maintainer-Entscheidung 2026-08-18: (1) remote_has_board wird nativ zuerst mit CLI-Fallback, also die Hauspolitik des restlichen Git.pm, statt weiter CLI-only. (2) Der ssh://-Fall kommt als Regressionstest in t/170, uebersprungen bei Git::Libgit2::version() < 1.9.3. Damit ist die im Ticket offen gelassene Policy-Frage beantwortet; die vier Doku-Stellen und remote_has_board werden zusammen gezogen.
Committet als f95abbe. Verifiziert vor dem Commit: prove -l t/ = 182 Dateien, 1272 Tests, Result PASS, exit 0, keine Skips (unabhaengig nachgelaufen, nicht nur vom Worker berichtet). ssh://-Fall in t/170 kommt bei 3s Budget nach 3.06s zurueck; t/203-remote-board-probe.t faellt gegen HEAD, beisst also. Offen geblieben und als #204 abgespalten: der DESCRIPTION-Absatz, der insteadOf faelschlich als CLI-only fuehrt -- libgit2 wendet die Rewrite-Regel selbst an.
